            "review_title": "Review at Pho Hung Vietnamese Beef Noodle Soup",
            "review_text": "our56\nMelbourne, Australia504 contributions\n0\nQuick and easy\nOct 2019\nBeing our first day in Ho Chi Minh we had already settled into our hotel, gone to a local coffee house and got our caffeine fix and had a stroll around the streets close to our hotel and we're getting a little hungry as it was just after midday. Suggestions were made of what to eat, mainly western takeaway but we decided to try some local cuisine being of course the pho. Not far from a hotel on our walk earlier we noticed this eatery and came back to try it out. Upon entering we were greeted by a young server who spoke a little English and directed us to our table near the window which was great for looking out and watching the street traffic go by. We ordered our drinks and pho or soup, my wife going for the plain chicken, my daughter the vegetable and my son and I had beef and pork. They came out soon after and you could see that they were very hot from the steam coming off the top as we waited a little for them to cool down we could smell the fresh herbs and spices that were used, they were fresh tasting and quite a good size, the noodles were nicely cooked not mushy, just right. The price for our overall meal was also quite cheap and for our first local cuisine experience this place gets a thumb's up from me and my family.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten May 30, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
